PE 745: Sum of Squares / 平方和

g(n) = largest perfect square dividing n
S(N) = sum_{n=1}^N g(n)

Small verification:
  S(10) = 24 (brute)  24 (fast)
  S(100) = 767 (brute)  767 (fast)

Derivation:
  Write n = a^2 * b with b squarefree, then g(n) = a^2
  S(N) = sum_{a^2*b≤N, b sqfree} a^2
       = sum_{t=1}^{√N} ⌊N/t^2⌋ * J_2(t)
  where J_2(t) = t^2 ∏_{p|t} (1 - 1/p^2) (Jordan's totient)

Target: S(10^14) mod 1e9+7
PE answer: 94586478
